title: Drag and drop with buttons
intro: A Grabber picks things up and puts them down with a button, so drag and drop works with a controller or the keys: a cursor moved with the stick, or a character who carries things about. No code.
project: Empty | Controller Sorter

chapter: A cursor that grabs | Gems, holes and a Grabber
create: Sprite
rename: Red Hole
set: Transform.Position.X = 3
set: Transform.Position.Y = 1
set: Sprite.Size = 1.4, 1.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #5A2A2A
add: DropTarget
set: DropTarget.Accepts = Red
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Blue Hole
set: Transform.Position.X = 3
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1
set: Sprite.Size = 1.4, 1.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #2A2A5A
add: DropTarget
set: DropTarget.Accepts = Blue
say: Two holes, one for red gems and one for blue, as in the mouse's drag and drop.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Red Gem
set: Transform.Position.X = -3
set: Transform.Position.Y = 1
set: Sprite.Tint = #E04848
set: Sprite.Order = 2
add: Draggable
set: Draggable.Kind = Red
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Blue Gem
set: Transform.Position.X = -3
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1
set: Sprite.Tint = #4870E0
set: Sprite.Order = 2
add: Draggable
set: Draggable.Kind = Blue
say: And a red gem and a blue one to put in them.
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Cursor
set: Sprite.Size = 1.2, 1.2
set: Sprite.Tint = #FFFFFF60
set: Sprite.Order = 1
add: Body
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.IsTrigger = true
add: GridMovement
set: GridMovement.Repeat = false
explain: component:GridMovement | A cursor | The cursor is a see-through square with a Grid Movement, so the arrow keys, the D-pad or the stick step it from square to square.
add: Grabber
explain: component:Grabber | Grabber | A Grabber picks up the draggable under it when its action is pressed, and puts it down where it's held on the next press.
explain: field:Grabber.Action | Action | The action is Interact: E or Enter on the keyboard, Y on a controller.
explain: field:Grabber.Reach | Reach | With nothing right under it, it reaches for the nearest thing within this distance.
explain: field:Grabber.HoldOffset | Hold Offset | And this is where it holds things. A cursor holds them in its middle; a character might carry a crate over its head, or in front of it.

chapter: Sorting with keys | Picking up, turning away, putting down
play
wait: 0.5
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
tap: Up
wait: 0.4
expectat: Cursor = -3, 1
explain: game | Highlight | Over the red gem, the gem lights up: that's what a press would pick up.
tap: E
wait: 0.4
say: Press, and the cursor has it.
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Down
wait: 0.25
tap: Down
wait: 0.4
expectat: Red Gem = 3, -1
tap: E
wait: 0.4
expectat: Red Gem = 3, -1
explain: game | Turned away | The blue hole doesn't take red gems, so the press does nothing and the cursor keeps holding it, rather than throwing it back across the board.
tap: Up
wait: 0.25
tap: Up
wait: 0.4
tap: E
wait: 0.5
expectat: Red Gem = 3, 1
say: Over the red hole, it goes in.
tap: Left
wait: 0.25
tap: Left
wait: 0.25
tap: Left
wait: 0.25
tap: Left
wait: 0.25
tap: Left
wait: 0.25
tap: Left
wait: 0.25
tap: Down
wait: 0.25
tap: Down
wait: 0.4
tap: E
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.25
tap: Right
wait: 0.4
tap: E
wait: 0.5
expectat: Blue Gem = 3, -1
stop
say: That's drag and drop with buttons. Put down on a full slot that swaps, the cursor picks up what was there, so a controller can sort an inventory. Give a top-down or platformer character a Grabber and it carries things about, and in a network game each player's grabber answers to their own controller.
